IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `gas-types`
IMPORT `gas-connection`
IMPORT `gas-cutoff`
IMPORT `gas-redress`

-- Gas Act 1986 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Seat: the gas consumer.
--
--   "Must the gas transporter connect my premises, or keep them connected,
--    and what can I be charged? Can my supplier cut off my gas or fit a
--    prepayment meter for debt, from when, and may its officer enter; can it
--    refuse to restore the supply? And if Ofgem acts on my supplier's breach,
--    can a redress order still be made, by when must I be paid, and what can
--    I recover on gas resold to me?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Gas consumer case` HAS
    `the connection`                                    IS A MAYBE `Connection request`
    `the cut-off`                                       IS A MAYBE `Cut-off case`
    `the contravention`                                 IS A MAYBE `Contravention facts`
    `the redress order`                                 IS A MAYBE `Redress order facts`
    `the resale`                                        IS A MAYBE `Resale facts`

DECLARE `Gas consumer position` HAS
    `connection`                                        IS A MAYBE `Connection outcome`
    `connection charge`                                 IS A MAYBE `Connection charge`
    `my pipe vests in the transporter`                  IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `earliest day the supply can be cut off`            IS A MAYBE DATE
    `supply may be cut off on the day`                  IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `officer may enter to cut off`                      IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `supplier may refuse to restore`                    IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `restoring it myself is an offence`                 IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `redress order can be made`                         IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `compliance date is lawful`                         IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `supplier's last day to appeal`                     IS A MAYBE DATE
    `interest on compensation runs from`                IS A MAYBE DATE
    `most compensation for the contravention`           IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `recoverable on resale`                             IS A MAYBE NUMBER

@ref ss 10-11, 30G-30O, 37, Sch 2B paras 7, 11, 19, 24, 28
@export default The gas consumer's position under the Gas Act 1986 (UK): whether the transporter must connect or keep connected my premises, what I can be charged, and whether my pipe vests in it (ss 10-11); from when my supplier may cut off my gas or fit a prepayment meter for debt, whether it may on the day, whether its officer may enter, whether restoring it myself is an offence, and whether it may refuse to restore it (Sch 2B paras 7, 11, 19, 24, 28); whether a consumer redress order can be made for its contravention, whether the order's compliance date is lawful, its last day to appeal, from when interest runs on unpaid compensation, and the most compensation in all (ss 30G-30O); and what I can recover on gas resold to me above the maximum price (s 37). Each is NOTHING where its facts are not given. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Gas consumer case`  @desc The connection request, any cut-off, the contravention and redress order, and any resale
GIVETH A `Gas consumer position`
`the gas consumer position for` c MEANS
    `Gas consumer position` WITH
        `connection`                                    IS
            CONSIDER c's `the connection`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST r  THEN JUST (`must the transporter connect` r)
        `connection charge`                             IS
            CONSIDER c's `the connection`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST r  THEN JUST (`the connection charge for` r)
        `my pipe vests in the transporter`              IS
            CONSIDER c's `the connection`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST r  THEN JUST (`my pipe vests in the transporter on connection for` r)
        `earliest day the supply can be cut off`        IS
            CONSIDER c's `the cut-off`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k  THEN `the earliest day my supply can be cut off for` k
        `supply may be cut off on the day`              IS
            CONSIDER c's `the cut-off`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k  THEN JUST (`my supply may be cut off on the day for` k)
        `officer may enter to cut off`                  IS
            CONSIDER c's `the cut-off`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k  THEN
                CONSIDER k's `the entry`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                WHEN JUST e  THEN JUST (`the officer may enter to cut off for` k `with` e)
        `supplier may refuse to restore`                IS
            CONSIDER c's `the cut-off`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k  THEN
                CONSIDER k's `the restoration`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                WHEN JUST r  THEN JUST (`the supplier may refuse to restore for` k `with` r)
        `restoring it myself is an offence`             IS
            CONSIDER c's `the cut-off`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k  THEN
                CONSIDER k's `the restoration`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                WHEN JUST r  THEN JUST (`restoring the supply myself is an offence for` r)
        `redress order can be made`                     IS
            CONSIDER c's `the contravention`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k  THEN JUST (`a consumer redress order can be made for` k)
        `compliance date is lawful`                     IS
            CONSIDER c's `the redress order`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST o  THEN JUST (`the compliance date is lawful for` o)
        `supplier's last day to appeal`                 IS
            CONSIDER c's `the redress order`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST o  THEN JUST (`the supplier's last day to appeal for` o)
        `interest on compensation runs from`            IS
            CONSIDER c's `the redress order`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST o  THEN `interest on my compensation runs from` o
        `most compensation for the contravention`       IS
            CONSIDER c's `the redress order`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST o  THEN JUST (`the most compensation for the contravention under` o)
        `recoverable on resale`                         IS
            CONSIDER c's `the resale`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST s  THEN `what I can recover on resale under` s
